---
/**
 * website/src/pages/privacy.astro — the privacy statement (website plan, Task W1.12;
 * reconciliation findings 16 and 18; decisions D93, D106 and W3.2's privacy defaults).
 *
 * The page a reader is owed once the site measures anything: what is collected, by what, when
 * it loads, how the answer is given and how it is taken back. It is also the page where the
 * choice is always available again — `Base.astro` is asked for `alwaysOffer` here, so the
 * banner appears on this page even for a visitor who already decided, which is what makes
 * consent withdrawable from the one page that says how (W1.12 step 3).
 *
 * **Every sentence about measurement is a fact the build holds, and nothing is invented.**
 * The page reads `site.yaml` through the content pipeline, exactly as the layout does, and
 * branches on `analytics.enabled`: with the flag off it says the site collects nothing, and
 * it names no vendor, because there is no vendor to name. With the flag on it states what the
 * site's own gate does — Google Analytics 4, one page view per page, no event and no user id,
 * Google Signals and ads personalisation off, GA4's own IP anonymisation — and it does not
 * restate Google's policy for Google. Three of its claims are held to the artifact by
 * `website/test/consent.mjs`: that no page carries a form or a field, that the tool it names
 * is the tool the build would load, and that the defaults it states are the ones the gate's
 * `config` call makes.
 *
 * **It is measured like every other page**, and D188's ceiling is 250 words: W3.2 turned the
 * flag on, so the branch a reader now sees is the one that has to fit, and the sentence about
 * the host's request logs gave way to the lead's link to `/security/` for it.
 *
 * The page carries no script of its own and no copy of the consent key: the banner is the
 * layout's, rendered here because this page asks for it. The styles are scoped, token-only
 * (no colour literal, so the palette stays W1.2's) and add no behaviour.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { loadSite } from '../content.ts'

// The facts, through the pipeline the layout uses: a site.yaml this page cannot read stops
// the build rather than shipping a statement about a configuration nobody checked (W1.3).
const site = loadSite()
const analyticsEnabled = site.facts.analytics.enabled
---

<Base title="Privacy" alwaysOffer>
  <article class="privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <p class="privacy-lead">
      What this website does with a visitor's browser. The Fugaro program's own posture is
      the <a href="/security/">security page</a>'s subject.
    </p>

    {analyticsEnabled ? (
      <>
        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          This site counts visits with <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>, Google's analytics
          service. If you accept, Google's script reports the page you are on to Google, which
          processes it for the site, and sets <strong>identifiers</strong> in your browser — a
          client id, in cookies or similar storage.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site's own code asks for one page view per page and nothing else: no event, no
          user id, Google Signals and ads personalisation off. Google Analytics 4 anonymises
          your IP address by default; what Google does beyond that is Google's own policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Consent</h2>
        <p>
          Google's script loads only after you accept, and never before: until then this page
          has asked Google for nothing. <strong>Accept</strong>, in the banner at the foot of
          the window, loads Google's script once, here; <strong>Decline</strong> loads
          nothing, now or on any later page.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dismissing the banner — Escape, or reading on — counts as a refusal. The answer is
          kept in this browser alone, under <code>fugaro:analytics-consent</code> in
          <code>localStorage</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          To withdraw, use the banner on this page: it always offers the choice again.
          Declining stops the next page loading anything; this one keeps what it already
          loaded.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It sets no cookie of its own.</li>
          <li>It has no account, no form, no comment box.</li>
          <li>
            It loads nothing from another origin except Google's script, and only after you
            accept.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <p>
          <strong>This site collects nothing.</strong> It is a set of static pages built from
          this repository's files: no account, no form, no comment box, and no code of the
          site's own running on a server. Nothing counts your visit, and nothing about it is
          sent anywhere. Should measurement ever be switched on, this page changes at the same
          time, and the site asks you first.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site has no analytics at all: nothing counts your visit, and no analytics
          script, cookie or identifier is involved in the page you are reading. There is no
          consent to give here, and nothing to withdraw.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It sets no cookie, and it loads nothing that could set one.</li>
          <li>
            It loads nothing from another origin — no font, no script, no image, no embedded
            player.
          </li>
          <li>It sells nothing, because it collects nothing to sell.</li>
        </ul>
      </>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Scoped, so nothing here can reach another page, and token-only: the palette is W1.2's and
     this file carries no colour literal (website/test/a11y.mjs refuses one outside :root). */
  .privacy {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--space-xl) var(--space-md) var(--space-3xl);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .privacy h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    margin: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-sm);
  }

  .privacy p,
  .privacy li {
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .privacy li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .privacy-lead {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xl);
  }

  .privacy ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy code {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 0 var(--space-3xs);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
